\subsection{Which Mechanisms Enable Adaptation After Route Disruption?}
\label{sec:exp-e2}

This study supplies the central mechanism evidence. The frozen
controlled-scenario protocol (version v8, formal revision r7) instantiates the
controlled-mechanism adapter with 8 households---each containing exactly two
decision-capable
adults, at least one dependent, and exactly one vehicle---over 10 steps with a
controlled primary-route closure. Five conditions (the full configuration and
four single-module removals) crossed with 12 seeds give 60 planned cells; all
60 completed with terminal status VALID (audit state
\textsc{complete\_valid}). The decision model is DeepSeek-V4-Flash at
high thinking effort with prompt
\linebreak[4]\texttt{carr\_s\_controlled\_resident\_v8}; the gateway records
6,693 calls with zero failures, zero fallbacks, and zero cache hits, for
75,850\,s of wall-clock time (mean 1,264\,s per cell). Opportunity is universal
for the gating checks: every one of the 60 cells records all 8 households with
a warning-exposed coordinator and all 16 decision-capable members holding a
pre-closure primary-route plan, so no manipulation check is credit-blind.

\begin{figure*}[t]
  \centering
