\emph{Manipulation checks.} All four modules pass their manipulation checks
with every seed pair in the predeclared direction
(\cref{tab:e2-manipulation}; \cref{fig:e2-effects}a). The memory check saturates at 1.000 with zero
variance: removal deletes the delivered-warning signal outright, so this check
verifies that the switch controls the intended signal rather than estimating a
graded behavioral effect. The feedback, planning, and interaction checks
estimate genuine behavioral rates---0.964, 0.906, and 0.938---and each clears
the predeclared direction in all 12 seed pairs with large standardized effects
($d_z$ between 9.62 and 19.44).

