The feedback mechanism replicates in direction for every model
(\cref{fig:e3-cross-model}a): both the
manipulation check and the downstream reduction in closed-route rejections hold
in 4/4 seed pairs per model (pooled $\bar{\Delta}$ 0.940 [0.892, 0.987] and
$-$6.527 [$-$7.414, $-$5.639]). The interaction manipulation check likewise
holds in 4/4 seed pairs for all seven models, and the downstream
coordinated-departure effect holds in 4/4 seed pairs for six of seven
(\cref{fig:e3-cross-model}b; pooled
$\bar{\Delta}$ 0.446 [0.350, 0.543]). The exception is GPT-5.4-mini, whose
coordinated-departure contrast is 0.031 [$-$0.068, 0.131] with only 1/4 seed
pairs in the predicted direction; the same model also shows the weakest
feedback manipulation effect (0.672) and the smallest downstream rejection
reduction ($-$1.688). Effect magnitudes thus remain model-dependent even when
directions agree---among the six consistent models, the interaction downstream
effect spans 0.375--0.781---so the cross-model study supports the signs, not
the sizes, of the two
mechanism effects, and per-model quantitative claims await the full seed count.
Condition levels vary even more than effect sizes: full-condition complete safe
household departure ranges from 0.031 (GPT-5.4-mini) to 0.781
(DeepSeek-V4-Flash), and decision-resident evacuation from 0.250 to
0.891. The model that fails the interaction downstream direction is also the
one with the lowest full-condition process quality, which is consistent with
attenuation rather than a sign reversal. Operationally, the 84 cells place
11,259 gateway calls with zero failures, fallbacks, or cache hits; per-cell
wall-clock time spans 56\,s (GPT-5.4-mini) to 1,227\,s
(DeepSeek-V4-Flash)---a 22-fold range across deployments, with
37,296\,s total. Metered gateway charges amount to 16.92 USD
(2.16--6.38 USD per model); the remaining three models were unmetered.
Wall-clock conflates serving load with model behavior and is
reported as operational evidence only.

\paragraph{Prompt-wording sensitivity}
A second robustness check varies prompt wording instead of the model. Two
paraphrases of the frozen controlled-scenario prompt---identical state JSON,
schema, mechanism switches, and action set, with only the instruction wording
changed---each run the same four seeds crossed with the full, without-feedback,
and without-interaction conditions (24 cells in all) on DeepSeek-V4-Flash at
temperature 0. Both paraphrases reproduce both determined effects on every
seed pair: the feedback downstream contrast averages $-$7.000 and $-$7.094
closed-route rejections per household under the two variants, against $-$6.844
under the original wording (4/4 seeds in the predicted direction in all three
wordings), and the interaction downstream contrast averages 0.938 and 0.875
coordinated departure, against 0.781 (again 4/4 throughout). Manipulation
checks pass in all 24 cells; the gateway records 3,010 completed calls with
zero failed and zero fallback calls at a metered cost of 11.36 USD. One variant
lane changed transport gateway mid-protocol under a frozen amendment that kept
the scientific design byte-identical and excluded the partial artifacts, and
per the frozen protocol both variants are reported regardless of interim
directions. This check bounds wording sensitivity within one model family; it
is not evidence of prompt invariance across models or providers, and it carries
the \textsc{complete\_valid} evidence state.

\section{Discussion}
\label{sec:discussion}

\emph{Mechanism function versus downstream necessity.} The central scientific
finding is the dissociation between the two: all four cognition and
communication modules pass their runner-aligned checks, yet only feedback and
interaction carry determined downstream effects in the controlled scenario, and
the condition levels show them playing different roles---feedback removal is
the only condition that makes dependents unsafe (0.055 versus 1.000), because
the household walks onto the closed route and cannot reroute, whereas
interaction removal leaves every dependent safe but eliminates the coordinated
form. Read at the domain level, the two determined channels are exactly the
ones that cross a state-ownership boundary: feedback reconnects world outcomes
to private belief, and interaction converts private intentions into household
coordination. The undetermined memory and planning contrasts admit three
readings---bounded opportunity in a single-closure, 10-step scenario, a
structural rather than graded memory check, and partial substitution between
modules that only a full factorial design could detect. The lesson transfers to
other generative-agent disaster systems
\cite{chen2025flare,dang2025fireagents,yang2026whenagents,sultimov2026respond}:
a mechanism switch validated only at its own interface can overstate necessity;
each switch needs both a manipulation check and a downstream estimand with an
explicit opportunity denominator. Throughout, the platform's contracts held
under full model-driven load, with complete message life-cycle accounting, zero
arbitration violations in every reported run, and the predeclared fallback gate
never approached.

\emph{Model dependence.} The directions of both determined effects replicate
across seven models of different families and sizes---feedback in all seven,
interaction downstream in six---while magnitudes vary by a factor of five for
feedback downstream, and full-condition process levels vary more still
(complete safe household departure spans 0.031--0.781 across models).
Mechanism-level conclusions about signs are therefore not an artifact of the
ablation's decision model, but quantitative transfer is model-dependent, so a
bounded cross-model pilot remains a necessary gate before any per-model
quantitative claim.

\emph{Boundaries and threats to validity.} All results come from one
Carr-informed controlled scenario archetype---one hazard trajectory, one
controlled closure, 8 households in the ablation and cross-model studies, 24
in the process study, and 100 in the two-seed scale demonstration---and do not
transfer to other hazards, scales, or network structures without new runs;
scale behavior in particular is established only within the demonstrated
100-household envelope. Carr-R references are directional only: the estimands
differ, the non-evacuator group contains 37 respondents, and the simulated
order-to-departure CDF is compressed toward zero relative to the survey, with
individual departure share well below the respondent-sample evacuation
proportion (\cref{tab:e1-dist}), so neither delay timing nor outcome level is
claimed to be behaviorally validated. The Carr-R test split has been opened for
a feature--outcome diagnostic and no longer serves as an analyst-blind
holdout. All five studies carry the \textsc{complete\_valid} evidence state
under the formal promotion audits, with numbers reported exactly as recorded in
the audit artifacts. No blinded human or expert plausibility review has been
completed, and scenario outputs remain computational artifacts rather than
representations of real persons.

\section{Conclusion}
\label{sec:conclusion}

We presented DisasterSociety, a generative agent-based simulation framework
that separates private resident cognition, household-shared constraints and
commitments, and authoritative world state, and connects them through an
event-driven kernel with typed intentions, lossy message life cycles, versioned
household commitments, and batched world arbitration, evaluated under a
claim--evidence protocol that maps each claim family to its appropriate
evidence. In the Carr-informed controlled case, an empirical-process study
completed all runs with zero constraint violations and process patterns
directionally consistent with the frozen survey reference, with level gaps
reported explicitly rather than tuned away, and a two-seed demonstration at 100
households reproduced the same process behavior with zero executed-party
violations at a metered cost near eleven dollars per run. A paired twelve-seed
ablation showed that memory, feedback, planning, and interaction are each
causally active at their own interfaces, while only feedback and interaction
carry determined downstream effects; a bounded seven-model study replicated the
directions of both effects, with one model exception on interaction downstream,
and two equivalent prompt paraphrases reproduced both effects on every seed.

Ongoing work extends cohort scale and hazard archetypes, extends the
cross-model study beyond its frozen four-seed design under a newly frozen seed
count, establishes a prospective or external holdout for individual-level
evaluation now that the original Carr-R test split has been opened for
diagnostics, and adds blinded human and expert judgment as an independent
reasonableness channel.


